1
00:00:02,650 --> 00:00:09,001
In 2025, more than half of new pump.fun tokens were sniped in the same block they were created.

2
00:00:09,301 --> 00:00:14,525
Across Solana launchpads, bundled wallets hold over a third of supply on average.

3
00:00:14,825 --> 00:00:19,074
Being first is the whole game. SlowCook makes being first worthless.

4
00:00:20,074 --> 00:00:27,354
Bids are sealed. When bidding closes, everyone reveals, and the contract sets one clearing price that every winner pays.

5
00:00:27,654 --> 00:00:32,077
Unsold supply is burned, and trading opens at exactly that price.

6
00:00:33,077 --> 00:00:38,685
In a simulation, we ran the same two hundred wallets through both designs, a thousand times.

7
00:00:38,985 --> 00:00:45,115
On a bonding curve, bots and a bundler take 40% of supply, and make over 400% by dumping.

8
00:00:45,415 --> 00:00:51,545
In SlowCook they take 11%, and lose about 9%, even when they can see all retail demand.

9
00:00:52,545 --> 00:00:54,763
This is a real launch on NEAR testnet.

10
00:00:55,063 --> 00:01:00,763
Twelve wallets committed sealed bids. Nobody could see a price, not bots and not the creator.

11
00:01:01,063 --> 00:01:03,919
A reveal with the wrong secret was rejected.

12
00:01:04,919 --> 00:01:09,726
Anyone can finalize. The contract fills bids from the highest price down.

13
00:01:10,026 --> 00:01:17,479
All 600,000 tokens sold at one clearing price, and the wallet that bid 7× higher paid exactly the same price per token.

14
00:01:17,779 --> 00:01:23,387
The pool opened at exactly that price, and the result matched our model's prediction made before launch.

15
00:01:24,387 --> 00:01:30,970
Then we scripted a sell-off. Six holders dumped, and the price fell to about a quarter of the clearing price.

16
00:01:31,270 --> 00:01:38,828
After three time-weighted intervals below the floor, the Floor Keeper bought back and burned tokens, using exactly its 10% cap.

17
00:01:39,128 --> 00:01:42,298
A second buyback in the same epoch was refused.

18
00:01:43,298 --> 00:01:47,605
The live page shows 103,215 tokens bought back and burned.

19
00:01:48,605 --> 00:01:53,934
Creator tokens are locked for at least 7 days. This demo uses 15 minutes.

20
00:01:54,234 --> 00:02:00,457
With the price held above clearing + 5%, the creator tried early. The contract refused.

21
00:02:00,757 --> 00:02:07,108
After the lock, tokens vest over time: 61,937 part-way through, the rest at the end.

22
00:02:08,108 --> 00:02:12,752
Every rule is a contract method with a test, and CI runs on every push.

23
00:02:13,052 --> 00:02:16,848
Live demo and code are linked below. Built at NEAR HACKATHON.
